{"facts":[{"text":"Belgrade is the capital.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mledoze/countries/blob/6031f5df137c41c76d180c55a0782185ae3ed05b/countries.json","sourceTitle":"mledoze/countries — country reference"},{"text":"Serbian is spoken here.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mledoze/countries/blob/6031f5df137c41c76d180c55a0782185ae3ed05b/countries.json","sourceTitle":"mledoze/countries — country reference"},{"text":"It is a landlocked country in Southeast Europe.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mledoze/countries/blob/6031f5df137c41c76d180c55a0782185ae3ed05b/countries.json","sourceTitle":"mledoze/countries — country reference"}],"culture":{"text":"Neighbourhood bakeries, called pekara, offer sweet and savoury pastries; a pastry with drinkable yoghurt is a familiar snack.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbia","sourceTitle":"Wikivoyage — Serbia"},"food":{"name":"Pljeskavica","text":"A grilled minced-meat patty often sold as a quick meal in a bread roll.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbia#Eat","sourceTitle":"Wikivoyage — Serbia — Eat"}}
